.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "August 2026" "Version 1.0" "Holberton School Manual"
.SH NAME
hsh \- Simple Unix command line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a UNIX command line interpreter that reads commands from standard input or from a file stream and executes them. It operates in both interactive and non-interactive modes.

.SS Interactive Mode
When executed without piped input, 
.B hsh
displays a prompt 
.B (#cisfun$ )
and waits for user input. Upon receiving a command, it parses the input, creates a child process using 
.BR fork (2), 
and executes the target executable with 
.BR execve (2).

.SS Non-Interactive Mode
When commands are piped into 
.B hsh
via standard input, no prompt is displayed. The shell reads sequentially until it encounters an 
.B EOF
(End-Of-File) condition or the 
.B exit 
command.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B hsh
uses the standard process environment array 
.I environ
passed via system execution to locate binaries and execute programs.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 upon successful termination or when receiving an explicit EOF condition (Ctrl+D). If a command is not found or fails to execute, the program continues running and returns the status of the child process.

.SH ERRORS
If a command cannot be executed, 
.B hsh 
prints an error message to standard error stream formatted as follows:
.RS
.B ./hsh: 1: command_name: not found
.RE

.SH BUGS
No known bugs at present.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR access (2),
.BR execve (2),
.BR fork (2),
.BR wait (2),
.BR getline (3)

